course: dictionary
lesson: 4195
title: When a name becomes a verb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be a name and an action at the same time. Google is the name of a large technology company and of its search engine, a website used to find information on the internet. Because it is a name, it starts with a capital letter.
explain: Google has also become a verb, a word for doing something. «I googled the answer» means I searched for it online. Verbs change their endings, so you can say google, googles, googled and googling. Brand names can work this way too: in British English, «to hoover» means to vacuum, from the Hoover company.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is used. In «ask Google, pet», Liam's gran means search for it online, and pet is a friendly word from north-east England for love or dear. To check, swap in the meaning: «ask search for it online, love» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Google is the name of a large technology company and its search engine.
fact: To google something means to search for it on the internet.
fact: «I googled the answer» means I searched online for the answer.
fact: A googol is the number 1 followed by 100 zeros, and the company's name was a play on that word.
fact: «Pet» (north-east England) means love or dear, as in «ask Google, pet».
exercise: In «Google Maps», what kind of word is Google? | A number | A verb meaning to search | *A name, a proper noun | A type of coin
exercise: «Ask Google, pet.» What does google mean here? | To make a cup of tea | *To search for the answer online | To go for a long walk | To pay for something with a card
exercise: «I googled the answer yesterday.» Which word is the past tense of google? | *googled | googles | googol | googling
test: «I googled the answer.» What does googled mean? | Drew a picture of the answer | *Searched for the answer on the internet | Wrote the answer on a card | Hid the answer under a book
test: What is a googol? | *The number 1 followed by 100 zeros | A type of computer | A brand of toy | A kind of map
exam: Which sentence uses google as a verb? | Sam's shoelace was made of wool. | Sam tied a shoelace with a bow. | Sam bought a new pair of shoes. | *Sam googled how to tie a shoelace.
